    rebuilding leaves every .cso that includes it STALE, with no warning and a
    successful build - so the engine runs yesterday's shader while the source says
    otherwise, and any measurement taken from it is wrong. That is not hypothetical:
    three rounds of an A/B on RC_BOUNCE_GAIN were all silently run against one
    binary, and read as "the feature does nothing".
    `AdditionalInputs` metadata on the FxCompile items does not fix it (tried, no
